## 🧪 Testing Standards (MANDATORY)

### Universal Testing Strategy

#### 1. Testing Pyramid
```
        ┌─────────────┐
        │   E2E Tests │  ← Few, High-Level
        └─────────────┘
       ┌─────────────────┐
       │ Integration     │  ← Some, Medium-Level
       │ Tests           │
       └─────────────────┘
    ┌───────────────────────┐
    │ Unit Tests           │  ← Many, Low-Level
    └───────────────────────┘
```

#### 2. Postman Testing Patterns
```typescript
// Test Scripts for Postman
pm.test("Response is successful", function () {
    pm.response.to.have.status(200);
    const jsonData = pm.response.json();
    pm.expect(jsonData.success).to.be.true;
});

// Store variables for chained requests
pm.collectionVariables.set("authToken", jsonData.data.accessToken);
pm.collectionVariables.set("userId", jsonData.data.user._id);

// Test authentication
pm.test("Authentication required", function () {
    pm.response.to.have.status(401);
    const jsonData = pm.response.json();
    pm.expect(jsonData.error.code).to.eql("UNAUTHORIZED");
});
```

#### 3. API Testing Checklist
- [ ] Health check endpoint
- [ ] User registration flow
- [ ] Email verification process
- [ ] Login with password
- [ ] Login with OTP
- [ ] JWT token validation
- [ ] Protected endpoint access
- [ ] Error handling scenarios
- [ ] Rate limiting behavior
- [ ] Input validation

#### 2. Test Categories
```typescript
// Unit Test Interface
interface UnitTest<T> {
  testName: string;
  arrange: () => T;
  act: (arrange: T) => Promise<any>;
  assert: (result: any, arrange: T) => void;
}

// Integration Test Interface
interface IntegrationTest {
  testName: string;
  setup: () => Promise<void>;
  execute: () => Promise<any>;
  cleanup: () => Promise<void>;
  assertions: (result: any) => void;
}

// E2E Test Interface
interface E2ETest {
  testName: string;
  scenario: string;
  steps: TestStep[];
  expectedResult: any;
}

interface TestStep {
  action: string;
  input?: any;
  expectedOutput?: any;
}
```

#### 3. Test Data Management
```typescript
// Universal Test Data Factory
interface TestDataFactory<T> {
  create(overrides?: Partial<T>): T;
  createMany(count: number, overrides?: Partial<T>): T[];
  createValid(): T;
  createInvalid(): Partial<T>;
}

// Mock Interface
interface Mock<T> {
  setup(): T;
  reset(): void;
  verify(): boolean;
}
```

### Testing Requirements
- Write unit tests for business logic
- Implement integration tests for API endpoints
- Use proper test data fixtures
- Maintain high test coverage
- Use Jest testing framework
- Mock external dependencies
- Aim for high test coverage

