## 🚀 Deployment & Operations (MANDATORY)

### Universal Deployment Standards

#### 1. Containerization
```dockerfile
# Universal Dockerfile Pattern
FROM node:18-alpine AS builder
WORKDIR /app
COPY package*.json ./
RUN npm ci --only=production
COPY . .
RUN npm run build

FROM node:18-alpine AS production
WORKDIR /app
COPY package*.json ./
RUN npm ci --only=production && npm cache clean --force
COPY --from=builder /app/dist ./dist
EXPOSE 3000
HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=3s --start-period=5s --retries=3 \
  CMD curl -f http://localhost:3000/health || exit 1
CMD ["node", "dist/main"]
```

#### 2. Health Checks
```typescript
// Universal Health Check Interface
interface HealthCheck {
  name: string;
  check(): Promise<HealthStatus>;
}

interface HealthStatus {
  status: 'healthy' | 'unhealthy' | 'degraded';
  message?: string;
  details?: Record<string, any>;
  timestamp: Date;
}

// Health Check Implementation
class DatabaseHealthCheck implements HealthCheck {
  name = 'database';
  
  async check(): Promise<HealthStatus> {
    try {
      await this.database.ping();
      return {
        status: 'healthy',
        message: 'Database connection successful',
        timestamp: new Date()
      };
    } catch (error) {
      return {
        status: 'unhealthy',
        message: 'Database connection failed',
        details: { error: error.message },
        timestamp: new Date()
      };
    }
  }
}
```

#### 3. Monitoring & Observability
```typescript
// Universal Metrics Interface
interface MetricsCollector {
  increment(metric: string, tags?: Record<string, string>): void;
  gauge(metric: string, value: number, tags?: Record<string, string>): void;
  histogram(metric: string, value: number, tags?: Record<string, string>): void;
  timer(metric: string, tags?: Record<string, string>): Timer;
}

interface Timer {
  stop(): void;
}
```

## 📝 Code Quality Standards (MANDATORY)

### TypeScript Usage
- Use strict TypeScript configuration
- Define interfaces for all data structures
- Use proper typing for all functions
- Avoid `any` type usage

### File Naming Conventions (Universal)
| Component | Convention | Example |
|-----------|------------|---------|
| **Files** | kebab-case | `user-service.ts`, `task-controller.ts` |
| **Classes** | PascalCase | `UserService`, `TaskController` |
| **Functions** | camelCase | `createUser()`, `getTaskById()` |
| **Constants** | UPPER_CASE | `MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS`, `DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE` |
| **Interfaces** | PascalCase | `User`, `CreateTaskRequest` |
| **Types** | PascalCase | `UserRole`, `TaskStatus` |
| **Enums** | PascalCase | `HttpStatus`, `ErrorCode` |

### Code Organization
- Use module aliases for clean imports
- Implement proper separation of concerns
- Keep functions small and focused
- Use descriptive variable and function names

### Documentation
- Comment complex business logic
- Use JSDoc for function documentation
- Maintain API documentation
- Keep README files updated

## 🎯 NestJS Specific Standards

### Module Organization
- Use feature modules for organization
- Import only necessary modules
- Export services that other modules need
- Use forRoot/forFeature pattern for database modules

### Controller Standards
- Keep controllers thin - only handle HTTP concerns
- Use DTOs for request/response validation
- Implement proper HTTP status codes
- Use appropriate decorators (@Get, @Post, @Put, @Delete)
- Handle errors gracefully

### Service Standards
- Contain all business logic
- Use dependency injection
- Make methods async when dealing with I/O
- Return proper types
- Handle errors appropriately

### DTO Standards
- Use class-validator decorators for validation
- Create separate DTOs for create/update operations
- Use class-transformer for data transformation

## 🗄️ MongoDB + Mongoose Standards

### Schema Design
- Use Mongoose schemas for MongoDB
- Define relationships with ObjectId references
- Use proper field types and validation
- Add indexes for performance

### Query Optimization
- Use proper indexing strategy
- Use aggregation pipelines for complex queries
- Handle MongoDB-specific error types
- Use transactions for multi-document operations

## 🔐 Authentication & Security Standards (MANDATORY)

### Authentication Patterns
- **JWT-based Authentication** with access and refresh tokens
- **OTP-based Login** for enhanced security
- **Email Verification** required for account activation
- **Password Hashing** with bcrypt (12+ rounds)
- **Rate Limiting** on authentication endpoints
- **Session Management** with proper token expiration

### Security Implementation
```typescript
// JWT Configuration
interface JWTConfig {
  secret: string;           // 32+ characters
  expiresIn: string;        // 15m for access tokens
  refreshExpiresIn: string; // 7d for refresh tokens
}

// Password Security
interface PasswordSecurity {
  bcryptRounds: number;     // 12-15 rounds
  minLength: number;        // 8 characters
  complexity: boolean;      // uppercase, lowercase, number, special char
}

// OTP Security
interface OTPSecurity {
  length: number;           // 6 digits
  expiresIn: number;        // 10 minutes
  maxAttempts: number;      // 3 attempts
  rateLimit: number;        // 1 minute cooldown
}
```

### Authentication Flow
1. **Registration** → Email verification required
2. **Login** → Password or OTP-based
3. **Token Management** → Access + Refresh tokens
4. **Password Reset** → Secure token-based reset
5. **Account Security** → Change password, logout

### Security Headers
```typescript
interface SecurityHeaders {
  'Authorization': 'Bearer <jwt-token>';
  'Content-Type': 'application/json';
  'X-Request-ID': 'unique-request-id';
  'X-API-Version': '1.0.0';
}
```

## 🎓 Educational Platform Specific Standards

### Core Entities
- **User**: Profile, progress, streaks, achievements, authentication
- **Subject**: Learning categories (Math, Science, etc.)
- **Topic**: Specific learning topics within subjects
- **Question**: MCQ questions with options and explanations
- **Progress**: User's learning progress tracking
- **Streak**: Daily study streak management
- **OTP**: One-time passwords for verification

### API Response Format
Always use consistent response format:
```typescript
interface ApiResponse<T> {
  success: boolean;
  data?: T;
  error?: {
    code: string;
    message: string;
    details?: any;
  };
  meta?: {
    timestamp: string;
    requestId: string;
    version: string;
  };
}
```

### Educational Platform Patterns
- **Progress Tracking**: Implement percentage-based progress calculation
- **Streak Management**: Use date-based streak calculation
- **Difficulty Levels**: Easy/Medium/Hard categorization
- **Gamification**: Achievements, milestones, and rewards
- **Learning Analytics**: Track study time, accuracy, completion rates
- **User Authentication**: Secure login with multiple methods
- **Data Privacy**: Protect user learning data

### MongoDB Collections Structure
```
users: { 
  _id, email, firstName, lastName, password, phoneNumber,
  role, status, isEmailVerified, isPhoneVerified,
  progress, streak, achievements, preferences, lastLoginAt
}
subjects: { _id, name, color, totalTopics, description, progress }
topics: { _id, subjectId, name, difficulty, estimatedTime, lessons }
questions: { _id, topicId, question, options, correctAnswer, explanation }
progress: { _id, userId, topicId, completedLessons, accuracy, lastStudied }
otps: { _id, code, identifier, type, status, expiresAt, attempts }
```

### Authentication Endpoints
```typescript
// Authentication Routes
POST   /api/auth/register           // User registration
POST   /api/auth/login              // Login with password
POST   /api/auth/login/otp          // Login with OTP
POST   /api/auth/request-login-otp  // Request login OTP
POST   /api/auth/verify-email       // Verify email with OTP
POST   /api/auth/forgot-password    // Request password reset
POST   /api/auth/reset-password     // Reset password
POST   /api/auth/change-password    // Change password
POST   /api/auth/refresh-token      // Refresh access token
GET    /api/auth/me                 // Get user profile

// OTP Management
POST   /api/auth/otp/request        // Request OTP
POST   /api/auth/otp/verify         // Verify OTP
POST   /api/auth/otp/resend         // Resend OTP
```

